  "content": "Formula: Euler's Formula\nExact Expression: e^{ix} = \\cos(x) + i \\sin(x)\nDefinitions: Fundamental bridge establishing the algebraic relationship between complex exponential functions and trigonometric functions.\nDerivation/Reference: Leonhard Euler, Introductio in analysin infinitorum (1748)\nExample: For x = pi: e^{i*pi} = cos(pi) + i*sin(pi) = -1 + 0 = -1 -> e^{i*pi} + 1 = 0\nDomain: trigonometry\nAssumptions: x in R (or generalized to C)\nCommon Errors: Inputting angle x in degrees instead of radians",
